   "title": "Low O2 saturation: get an ARTERIAL gas. PaO2 < 80? Then: is the A-a GRADIENT normal?",
   "lines": [
    "arterial (PaO2) and alveolar (PAO2) O2 · alveolar gas: PAO2 = PIO2 − PaCO2 / 0.8 (room air: 150 − 1.25 × PaCO2)",
    "alveolar-arterial (A-a) gradient = PAO2 − PaO2 · normal ≤ age / 4 + 4 · a venous gas does not help"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_n",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 468,
   "h": 80,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "A-a gradient NORMAL: too little O2 REACHES the alveoli",
   "lines": [
